cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Concord in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "Concord: collaborative development of open data standards"
abstract: >-
  Concord is where working groups design open data standards together. Each
  standard is a strict OWL 2 ontology. Requirements come in from interviews,
  meeting transcripts and coding agents, and every proposed change is checked,
  then reviewed or voted on under rules the group sets for itself, without
  needing a meeting.
authors:
  - family-names: Wright
    given-names: Jesse
    affiliation: Open Data Institute
repository-code: "https://github.com/standards-concord/standards-concord"
url: "https://standards-concord.vercel.app"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - open data standards
  - ontology engineering
  - OWL 2
  - collaborative ontology development
  - deliberation
  - governance
  - linked data
  - semantic web
